WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.860
Good morning, Lady Draconness.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.540
How are you feeling?

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.360
The same.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.540
Lady Draconness, please have the surgery.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.490
This goes without saying for Lady Cthulhy, 
but Dr. Glenn is also very trustworthy.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.330
I'm sure he'll...

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.000
It's all right, Kunai.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.000
This is my fate.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.230
<b>Monster Girl Doctor</b>

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.980
Case 10         The Self-Deprecating Cyclops

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.980
Hello.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.500
Hey there, Memé.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.300
A h-human!

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.810
Oh, it's just you, Dr. Glenn.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.870
Sorry, did I scare you?

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.620
J-Just a little.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.390
It still shocks me when 
I see someone with two eyes.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.110
I can imagine.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.680
Though, biologically, it's rarer 
to find someone with one eye.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.720
R-Right. I'm sure cyclopes 
are pretty scary.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.220
I-It's unusual for you to come 
all the way to the workshop.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.950
There's something I needed the boss to make.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.110
Have you been well, Memé?

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.670
Not really. Stiff shoulders and 
lower back pain come with the job.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:07.790
Not to mention, I'm pale, and I've 
got a dark circle around my eye.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.070
You want to say that I look ill, right?

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.580
I didn't say anything like that.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.190
It's fine, it's just the truth.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.600
I run into people all the time, 
almost get run over by carriages...

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.440
Well, cyclopes have problems 
with depth perception.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.730
Be careful, okay?

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.850
I-I know that, dummy!

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.940
Whoa. Are you okay?

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:30.550
T-Too close! Y-You're too close!

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:35.640
A loincloth?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:48.160
I can't believe you saw that... 
Now I can never get married.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.680
Not that anyone would want 
to marry me, anyway...

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.160
Watch where you're going, 
or you'll run into something again.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.400
Boss, you've got a visitor.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.630
Ah, hey there, Doc.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:05.440
What brings you here? 
I've already delivered this month's tools.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.400
Well, you see...

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.050
Surgery for Lady Draconness, eh?

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.690
Yes. The head doctor at Central Hospital, 
Dr. Cthulhy, and I will perform it.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.810
We need tools that could 
be used in this surgery.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.850
We'll have to start by gathering materials.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:26.560
This is gonna cost a lot of time and money.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.250
Don't worry about that.
The Central Hospital will foot the bill.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.680
As for the delivery... We'd like it
within a month, at the latest.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.760
A month, eh?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.170
All right, got it. I'll accept.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.220
Really?

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.220
Yeah. I'll put my pride as a 
cyclops on the line for this.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.240
However...

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.220
I can't make any promises about the needles.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:54.590
It won't be easy to make something as 
small as a suture needle strong enough

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.550
to get through dragon scales.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.690
I can't guarantee that by the date.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.380
But you'll make it?

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:05.490
Of course we will. 
I'll have one of my best workers on it.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.620
But I still can't make any guarantees.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.990
Please.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.400
Memé, wanna try making the needle?

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.320
Huh?!

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.920
M-M-Me?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.470
Yeah, it's gonna be small, 
but it'll be a lot of work.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.270
N-No way! I can't do that, Boss!

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.070
Why would you ask someone like me 
to make something so important?!

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:31.050
Oh, come on. You're about ready to 
handle making something on your own.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.360
Y-You say that, but I know your true motive!

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.770
You just want to put all the blame 
on me when the surgery fails, right?

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.830
The surgery will fail because of my needle.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:43.530
The city will be thrown into chaos, 
the tabloids will expose my private life...

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.180
Then I won't be able to 
stay in this city anymore!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:49.550
You really don't know how 
to be positive, do ya?

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.280
Stop yer yappin' and just do it!

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:52.830
But...

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.910
I'm counting on you, Memé.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.630
Not you, too, Dr. Glenn!

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.180
What in the world...

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.560
What in the world <i>is</i> this?

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:09.320
You're too violent. Dr. Glenn is better.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.670
What did you expect? I'm an amateur.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.860
Still, I never expected 
to find you working here.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.810
I thought it was some kind of joke.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.400
This is too important to be a joke!

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.280
Though I kinda regret agreeing to it...

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.530
Well, do your best. 
Here, I brought you some water.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.960
Sapphee, I'm tired. Get me some booze.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:38.470
Absolutely not. No alcohol for a while.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.220
So harsh...

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:45.510
Dr. Glenn, about Lady Draconness...

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:48.490
She's still being stubborn.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:53.020
I keep trying to convince her, but she's 
still reluctant about the surgery.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.850
I guess I'm not surprised.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.350
Why is she so against it?

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.850
She says that this is her fate. 
That it's just her time to go.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:07.100
Lady Draconness despises the long history 
of fighting between humans and monsters,

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.310
and gave her all to establish 
this city where both could live.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:14.710
She believed that this was her mission.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:19.500
Lindworm has grown into one of the 
largest cities on this continent.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.710
So she feels that her mission is done.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.120
She believes it may as well be 
her fate to die of an illness.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.820
But we have to continue
trying to persuade her.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.670
I'll accompany you next time.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:35.090
Right. If we continue to convince 
her, she should eventually...

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:36.090
You think so?

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:41.980
Keep sayin' the same thing, and she 
might just shut you out even more.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:45.320
Twisting threads together 
makes them stronger,

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.980
but also harder to use.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.750
You can't just increase your 
numbers and push harder.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.850
Sometimes you have to take a step back.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.690
What should we do, then?

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:57.460
If goin' from the front doesn't work, 
just add some color from the back.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.470
You're an expert at that, aren't you, Doctor?

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.990
Huh? No, I don't have experience in...

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.270
What are you talkin' about?

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:09.040
Look at how red you make 
Sapphee's face all the time!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.000
How do you get it to be so brilliantly red?

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.270
Arahnia!

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.360
See? She turned red!

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.590
Come back here!

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:19.140
Looks like they got you there, Dr. Glenn.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.610
I'm absolutely in stitches.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:25.060
If you still have a sense of 
humor, you should be fine.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.470
This isn't funny!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.360
It's always so hot here.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.980
You should probably break 
that habit of yours, Doctor.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.960
This calms me down.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:40.710
Would you like a bite, Glenn?

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.460
Trying to get others to eat it is 
also a terrible habit of yours.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.080
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:49.330
Here are the final prototypes 
for the surgical tools.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.400
Take a look.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:00.430
It's very sharp. I like it.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.900
P-Please don't cut off your own 
tentacle to find that out.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:07.220
This should be able to 
cut through dragon scales.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:08.890
Go ahead and mass-produce them.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:12.150
Leave it to us. 
We'll get them to you on time.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.150
What are these?

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.910
Ah, those needles aren't done yet.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.690
Memé's been trying a few things,

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:25.300
but she's having trouble 
coming up with something usable.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.540
She's been spending all her 
time in the drafting room.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.120
I'll try to give her some ideas 
for the needles, too,

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.030
but I really want her to handle this herself.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.340
I want her to gain some confidence.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.110
I know.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:42.830
If possible, I'd like Memé 
to make them, as well.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:50.240
You must be fast, bold, and careful 
when making your incision.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.280
R-Right.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.290
The tissue fluid's oozing out.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.110
Go any slower and your 
patient's going to die.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.090
Right!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:00.740
<i>My first surgery was pretty major, too.</i>

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:06.620
What's this, Glenn? Did you finally 
realize how beautiful I am?

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:11.240
No, I was just thinking 
how hard you were on us.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.400
I wish that wasn't in the past tense.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.670
I'm still plenty hard on you now.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.430
Want a bite?

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.500
No, thank you.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:30.260
No, this won't do, either.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.570
I need to think of something else.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.780
Something that's strong enough 
and that we can mass-produce.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.040
<b>Monster Girl Doctor</b>

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:56.230
Illy, we told you that you need to 
deliver letters through the front—

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.680
Now's not the time for that!

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.380
Urgent message from the Kuklo Workshop!

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.730
They said some girl named Memé 
just suddenly collapsed there!

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:06.230
Memé!

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.720
Oh, Doc!

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:11.660
I came to see how things were going 
in here, and I found her like this...

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:13.160
Please calm down.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.370
I'll see how she's doing.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.460
She's breathing.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.830
Memé, can you hear me? 
Answer me if you can.

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.490
Her pulse is weak, but it's there.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.380
I want to make it easier for her to breathe.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.370
Sapphee.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:28.210
Right.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:35.830
Doc, is Memé sick or something?

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.470
Nothing gave me that indication,

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:42.300
but considering how hot it gets 
in here, it could be heatstroke.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.250
For now, let's get her somewhere 
cool so she can rest.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.470
Could you carry her to the clinic?

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.840
Sure! Leave it to us. 
We'll get a stretcher ready.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.740
Needles...

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.750
I have to make... the needles...

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.750
<i>I always wanted to be an artisan.</i>

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.090
<i>I wanted to make peaceful things 
in this now-peaceful land.</i>

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:17.690
<i>Something other than axes and knives 
that would remind us of the war...</i>

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.890
<i>The boss and the others 
felt the same way, too.</i>

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.700
<i>And that's when she came along.</i>

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.740
I heard that you cyclopes once made weapons,

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:34.280
but the Central Hospital would like 
you to make medical tools.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:38.730
I'm sure the techniques you've honed 
making weapons will be useful.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:43.110
But these tools will be used to save lives.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:49.120
I promise you that your techniques will 
save many more lives than those lost

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.240
in the bloodshed of the war.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:13:00.130
<i>She was able to shake us to 
our cores with just her words.</i>

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:04.580
<i>"I want to be an artisan who'll 
be needed by others someday!"</i>

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.750
<i>That's how I felt.</i>

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:11.740
<i>I waited so long for a chance to 
do a job that could help her...</i>

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:13.530
<i>For the day I could save someone.</i>

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:17.460
<i>So... So...</i>

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:19.600
<i>So...!</i>

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.090
Wait, where am I?

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.780
Are you awake?

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.110
Doctor...

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:31.100
I shouldn't be laying down like this!

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:34.290
No, don't. You need to keep resting.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.750
I feel nauseous, Doctor.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.030
There, there. You'll be okay.

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:42.310
My, Doctor. You sound so kind.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:46.680
Much nicer than when he talks to us.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:51.980
But Memé is a hard worker, 
so of course he likes her.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.670
I work hard, too!

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:55.980
But you drink, Sapphee.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.310
What's that got to do with anything?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:02.290
What happened to me? 
Why am I at your clinic?

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.080
You collapsed at the workshop.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:08.050
W-Wait, I did?! But why?

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:10.360
We're about to find that out.

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:11.980
Okay...

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.070
Wh-Why am I—

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:21.110
Oh, sorry... It was an emergency, 
so I cut open your top.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.330
I'll pay you back for it.

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:25.020
Th-That's not the problem here!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.800
You saw me! You saw me! You saw me!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.220
You didn't just see my underwear, 
you saw my chest, too!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.470
Her underwear? What does 
she mean by that, Doctor?

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.620
Uh, that happened a while back...

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.470
Go ahead and use this.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:42.850
I made it quickly, but it should 
fit Memé just perfectly.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.240
Th-Thank you, Arahnia.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.890
Think nothing of it.

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:49.760
Let me know the next time you 
want another Gothic Lolita outfit.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:52.540
Th-That was supposed to be a secret!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.740
Oh, dear. So sorry.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.410
Also, my dear Doctor,

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:00.770
if you cut open a girl's top, 
you need to show more consideration.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.010
Clothes are everything for a lady!

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.830
I-I'll be more careful in the future...

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.790
Don't worry. We're almost done.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.560
Should we get her some eyedrops?

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.960
No, it's not her eye.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.940
More importantly, could you prepare 
some herbs that'll calm her nerves?

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.610
Yes, right away.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.850
So, what kind of ailment does she have?

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.420
Well, she's not exactly sick.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.860
Memé was just... tipsy.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:37.400
Tipsy?! Memé, you were drinking?!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.650
O-Of course not! I wasn't!

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:40.740
That's not it.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:44.870
She wasn't intoxicated from alcohol. 
It's something like motion sickness.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:46.860
Motion sickness?

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:53.470
Since cyclopes have such excellent eyesight, 
the semicircular canals in her ears

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:57.630
that sense spinning or movement 
are quite easily stressed.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.420
I feel sick...

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.020
I'm fine!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.190
Riding in a carriage, staring at a waterwheel,

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:06.020
and repetitive back-and-forth 
or up-and-down movement

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.280
can cause stress to the semicircular canals,

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.600
making you feel as if things 
are spinning in front of you,

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.270
making your vision hazy, 
or even causing hallucinations.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:17.790
But she was in the workshop, wasn't she?

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.490
There aren't any carriages 
or waterwheels there.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:21.990
That's the question here.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:25.870
Memé, what were you staring 
at in the drafting room?

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:28.340
Here you go.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.710
Oh... Thank you.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:41.520
I was making needles.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.970
New needles made in a 
completely different way.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:49.330
Since I had this chance, I wanted 
to show all of you that I could.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:54.080
I'm a failure of a cyclops who 
can never do anything right...

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:58.070
But I... But I really worked hard this time!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.700
All right. Let's head over right now.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:06.510
I'm really sorry about all this, Boss.

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:08.630
I passed out and caused 
trouble for everyone...

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.620
Okay, okay. It's all right, 
as long as you're better now.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:14.880
I'm the one who pushed you too hard.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.350
Thanks for this, Doc.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:22.190
I'll personally make sure 
the needles get done.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:26.930
No, Boss. I think Memé has 
the needles all figured out.

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:28.440
You do?

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.450
This machine... This is what helped me out.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:43.190
A... spinning wheel?

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:48.720
Y-Yes. At first, I was just molding 
and strengthening iron into needles...

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:52.810
But it still wasn't strong enough 
to get through dragon scales.

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:55.950
I changed up the ingredients and 
tried a few different things, but...

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:58.890
The sturdier ones are more 
complicated to make,

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.750
so we won't be able to mass-produce them.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.620
Yeah, I figured...

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:05.400
And that's how I thought of using this.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.390
This machine stretches materials by turning,

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:13.140
meaning we can stretch out 
hard steel to make wire.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:16.150
If we stretch and cut 
the wire into small pieces,

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:18.670
we can make them into suture 
needles that can be mass-produced.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:22.540
They're hard to begin with,
so they shouldn't break.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.260
Considering how strong steel is,

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:27.130
you might not be able to sew a 
blood vessel more than ten times,

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:30.160
but with this method, we'll be able 
to make the amount you need,

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:32.440
so it's fine if you have to keep replacing them!

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:36.250
I thought this would help out 
with the dragon's surgery.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.480
I mean, you may never use something 
that someone like me made,

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:43.500
but I figured you might use them, 
even though you probably don't want to,

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.950
so I...

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.470
Memé, you're really close...

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:52.660
No!

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:54.580
Er, that might be a bit too far...

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.950
Finding the right balance is hard, isn't it?

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:05.080
I see. It's really sturdy, despite being so thin.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.120
It's actually quite durable.

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:11.920
We'll be able to make more than 
enough for the order with these.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.270
Right, Doctor?

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.200
Yes, I think this will work.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.350
Not only will this get through dragon scales,

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:20.040
but it should be able to get into 
the gaps between them, too.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:24.730
Well done, Memé. You're definitely 
on track to openin' your own workshop.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:28.450
P-Please don't compliment me. 
I'm sure you have ulterior motives.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:30.870
You'll probably want something later.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:32.820
Of course we won't.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.840
Yes. We're truly grateful from 
the bottom of our hearts.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.190
Thank you.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.190
Anyway...

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:49.320
You stared at this long enough 
that you got dizzy and passed out?

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.000
That's how invested she was in her work.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:59.710
After I discuss this with Dr. Cthulhy, 
I'll have you mass-produce these.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:02.700
O-Okay... That's fine...

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.480
U-Um, Dr. Glenn!

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:09.460
Yes, what is it?

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:14.740
Th-Thank you for letting me d-do this job...

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.350
You're welcome.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.970
Also, from now on,

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:22.450
make sure to hold your head up high so 
you don't run into things when you walk.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.750
What? Do I have to?

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:25.490
Yup.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:31.800
B-But my eyebrow is weird... d-don't you think?

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:34.300
It's way too far to the left and slanty...

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.080
So I just felt pathetic...

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:40.580
Don't worry. Eyebrow shapes 
are unique to each person,

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:42.970
and your pupil and iris are just fine, too.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.710
There's nothing weird about it at all.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:49.780
Y-You perverted, sexually harassing doctor!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.970
How dare you use your wiles on me?!

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.340
Wait, what?

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:56.840
I-I-I'll take you to court!

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:01.490
There must be better ways for 
her to deal with her shyness...

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:04.000
Maybe that was too much for her.

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.680
Who's to say?

00:22:37.860 --> 00:22:39.040
Huh?

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:41.960
Is something the matter?

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:47.230
Well, I was looking for my stethoscope, 
and I found it here.

00:22:47.230 --> 00:22:49.400
I wonder if I put it here without noticing...

00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:54.640
So you're taking that off?

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.740
I'm sorry. I know you gave it to me,

00:22:57.740 --> 00:23:02.600
but it doesn't feel right having it when 
I'm seeing Lady Skadi, who's a dragon.

00:23:03.010 --> 00:23:04.860
Could you put it in my room for me?

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:07.940
Of course, Doctor.

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:10.200
Well, I'm off.

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:11.280
Be careful.

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:13.180
Safe travels!

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.170
Is he gonna be able to convince her?

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:18.810
That's up to Lady Skadi herself.

00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:22.290
But I'm sure the doctor will get her to agree.

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:26.040
What a dutiful, loving wifey you are. 
You trust each other so much.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:28.790
Mind your own business.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Case 11       Lindworm's Major Operation

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:39.530
Case 11: "Lindworm's Major Operation."
